					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: MODULATING THE RADIUS\n\nIn this example we use the Linear node to create a collection of 10 values running from 0 to 1.\nWith this we modulate the radius inlet of the Circle node.\nBecause the signal from the Linear node is instanced, the Circle and Edge node are automatically updated by Wire to match the incoming collection size. \n\nTry playing with the min, max and size inlets on the Linear node and watch what happens."
					}
				},
