						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 5:  ATTRIBUTE SIZE\n\nWelcome to the final boss level of the Linear node.\nHere we have expanded the example again with a Integer In slider (renamed Size) to modulate the size of both Linear nodes.\nThe Size slider also goes through a Map node which makes sure the size of the rectangles decrease as more rectangles are added.\n\nThis example really demonstrates the power of the attribute flow.\nWe set a size, we calculate the linear collection only once and Wire will update the amount of shapes for you."
					}
				},
